  "usage_note": "When **apart** is followed by **from**, the two words work together as a preposition meaning *except* or *as well as* (*apart from Sam, everyone came*), a separate entry. **Apart** is one word; **a part** (two words) means one piece of something.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "It is apart of my job.",
      "correct": "It is a part of my job.",
      "note": "**A part** (two words) means one piece of a whole; **apart** (one word) means separated."
    }
  ],
